Subproblem 1: Identify which features or feature groups (e.g., shape density, perimeter-area relationships, symmetry moments, and axis variability) are most relevant for distinguishing vehicle types when silhouettes are viewed from various angles.
Answer 1: To distinguish vehicle types when silhouettes are viewed from different angles, the most relevant feature groups are:

